  "text_md": "**March 9-13, 2020 |** <u>www.ceraweek.com</u>\n\n# Media Registration is Now Open for CERAWeek by IHS Markit 2020\n\n**Applications for media registration can be submitted at the following link:** **[https://bit.ly/2LoeSGU**](https://bit.ly/2LoeSGU**)\n\nAll members of the media interested in attending CERAWeek 2020 are required to apply for accreditation. **Complete details related to media registration are included below in this email.**\n\n## About CERAWeek 2020\n\nCERAWeek 2020 will kick off Monday, March 9 at the Hilton Americas-Houston. CERAWeek by IHS Markit is the premier annual international gathering of energy industry leaders, experts, government officials and policymakers, leaders from the technology, financial and industrial communities – and energy technology innovators. Chaired by Daniel Yergin, CERAWeek 2020 will be the event’s 39th installment. Visit <u>www.ceraweek.com</u> for the most up-to-date event information and follow us via <u>@CERAWeek</u>. Listed session times, topics and speakers are subject to change.\n\n## Media Registration Details:\n\nAll members of the media interested in attending CERAWeek 2020 are required to apply for accreditation. Journalists should submit their request for media registration at the following link: <u>[https://bit.ly/2LoeSGU](https://bit.ly/2LoeSGU)</u> As always, the CERAWeek Media Relations Team is happy to provide a designated media work room as part of our conference-wide efforts to make journalists’ experiences convenient and productive at the conference. **CERAWeek 2020 Media Work Room Amenities:**\n\n- Fully-staffed Media Work Room adjacent to the CERAWeek Briefing Room\n",
